# Array-based recharge (READASARRAYS).  The SUMMA coupler overwrites the RECHARGE
# array in memory (SAGEHEN/RCHA/RECHARGE) every time step with the regridded SUMMA
# soil-column drainage, in m/s.  The constant below is only the pre-coupling default
# used when running mf6 stand-alone; it is a small non-zero background rate so the
# water table does not collapse (and diverge) over a long zero-recharge stand-alone run.
BEGIN OPTIONS
  READASARRAYS
  SAVE_FLOWS
END OPTIONS

# PERIOD 1 is the steady-state spin-up: this array IS used, and should be a climatological
# mean recharge for the basin.  The coupler does not overwrite it, because equilibrating an
# aquifer against one hour of instantaneous SUMMA drainage would be meaningless.
BEGIN PERIOD 1
  RECHARGE
    CONSTANT  1.0e-8
END PERIOD

# PERIOD 2 is the coupled transient period: the coupler overwrites this array every step
# with SUMMA's regridded soil drainage, so the value here is only a placeholder.
BEGIN PERIOD 2
  RECHARGE
    CONSTANT  1.0e-8
END PERIOD
